{
    "_comment": "Per-mode cluster composition, read at runtime by main.qml (Qt.resolvedUrl + XMLHttpRequest). Each mode maps to { title, items[] }. 'kind' picks the QML component (pie | multipie | bargrid | rate | text) via main.qml's kindComponent() map; 'metric' picks which snapshot field(s) that component instance reads via main.qml's metric* helper functions. Adding a mode/item here is the intended way to grow this widget -- it must not require another hardcoded Loader block in main.qml. 2026-08-11: every cluster now follows ONE shape -- a headline pie carrying the single number worth reading at a glance, then the bars that break it down. Before this, storage led with bars and no total, mem led with a ring and no absolute figures, and psi/guard were bare grids.",
